0219: EFB-copy readback map callbacks make no Dawn call (render-loop deadlock)

The readback MapAsync callback (AllowSpontaneous) called GetConstMappedRange and Unmap. Spontaneous
callbacks run inside whatever Dawn call notices the map; the present-timing waiter thread (0197/0216)
polls Instance::WaitAny every ~0.25 ms, so the callback often ran there. When the render worker was
at the same time inside a Dawn call holding the device lock and waiting for that event to finish,
the callback's Unmap waited for the device lock and the render worker waited for the callback: the
render loop stopped for good (the main thread in acquire_frame_slot's wait_for_gpu_progress, the
game thread in VISetNextFrameBuffer). Seen in LM's frame interpolation runs in Bogmire's arena after
about 3 minutes (LM_HANG_DUMP stacks: present_timing::waiter -> Dawn -> efb_ram map callback ->
Dawn -> Mtx_lock; render worker in Dawn Cnd_wait).

Now the callback only records the status and queues the readback (leaf lock); finish_maps copies
the mapped bytes out and unmaps, holding no lock, on the render worker after each frame
(gfx::after_submit) and in aurora_efb_ram_apply. The readback pool keeps each buffer's size so
acquire_readback_buffer makes no Dawn call (GetSize) under g_poolMutex.

